# HPC-first job execution

For this project (`/common/omarmlab/members/anh/panda_project`):

- **Never** run long or heavy jobs on the login node (`esplhpccompbio-lv01`).
- **Always** submit via `sbatch scripts/slurm_*.sh` on partition `defq` (CPU) or `gpu` (train/eval).
- Opt3 train: `scripts/slurm_train_opt3_slidebag.sh` — Omar-6 recipe only (see below).
- Slurm headers: `#SBATCH --partition=gpu` or `defq`, `-o %j.out` / logs, `-e %j.err`
- Env: `module load miniconda3/23.11.0-2`, `conda activate wsi_seg`, `source .env.hpc`

## Omar-6 Opt3 recipe (locked)

- Tag `opt3_omar6_grouped_soft01`
- `--min-area-pct 0` (no 5% gate)
- `--min-slide-patches 5` (n<5 hard-skip L_slide/L_grade)
- `--adjacent-soft-alpha 0.1 --include-benign-soft` (benign↔G3↔G4↔G5)
- LoRA QKV, `--decode-norm gn`, `--live-patches 64`, `--lambda-slide-warmup`
- **Every epoch** saved (`--save-every 1`; never every-5)
- No patch cap (`MAX_PATCHES_PER_SLIDE=0`)
- Prefer `--time=30-00:00:00` on `gpu`+`normal`

## Never kill a live Opt3 / H200 train

- **Never `scancel` a job in state `R`** for Opt3 / H200 / the current run tag.
- Dual-queue is OK: 2× **RUNNING** + 4× **PENDING**. Cancel the 2× only after the 4× is **actually RUNNING**, via SIGTERM.
- `scripts/monitor_opt3_h200.sh` must not scancel RUNNING jobs.
